      "time_horizon": "quarter",
      "rationale": "JNJ presents a rare case of all three pillars aligning negatively. Pillar 1 (Fundamentals): While revenue growth is solid (+6.6% YoY to $25.31B), earnings are flat (EPS $2.27 vs $2.29 YoY) due to margin compression \u2014 net margin fell from 25% to 21.5%, ROE declined from 0.289 to 0.248. The incremental revenue dollar is flowing to cost, not profit. Stelara's 56% biosimilar-driven decline is a structural headwind, and the Tremfya transition is not yet complete (immunology declined 4.6% operationally). Pillar 2 (Valuation): PE of 30.1x sits at the absolute top of its 365-day range (17.6\u201331.1x), representing ~67% multiple expansion over the past year \u2014 all while fundamentals deteriorated. Earnings yield of 3.3% is 140bp below the 10-year Treasury yield of 4.71%, implying a negative equity risk premium for a mature healthcare name. P/B expanded from 5.2x to 7.4x while ROE compressed. The market is paying a historically elevated multiple for historically diminished returns. Pillar 3 (Near-term catalyst): The OTTAVA FDA approval is a positive but is already priced in (stock popped ~2%). The more material near-term risk is continued Stelara erosion, restructuring, restructuring restructuring restructuring$FTC restructuring, restructuring costs restructuring restructuring$1.1",
